# deskidle.ps2 - ⛔ THE NEGATIVE CONTROL.
#
# The same ROM, the same card, the same `desk`, and a mouse that walks the
# whole length of the menu bar - over both titles, twice - and NEVER PRESSES
# A BUTTON.  The menu must stay shut and the picture must not change.
#
# Without this every claim in run-v3desk.sh is satisfied by a program that
# draws a pull-down on a timer and highlights its items in turn.
#
# ⚠ THE WALK IS AT y = 1, NOT y = 8, and that is the control's own
# correctness rather than tidiness: video3 composites the pointer as a
# 16 x 16 sprite whose hot spot is its top left, so a pointer at y = 8
# covers rows 8..23 - and rows 19..23 are inside the pull-down's rectangle,
# which is the rectangle this control asserts never changes.  At y = 1 the
# sprite stops at row 16 and the assertion is about the desktop alone.
origin 320 240

at 1.500    move to 20 1
+0.700      move to 100 1
+0.700      move to 168 1
+0.700      move to 300 1
+0.700      move to 100 1
+0.700      move to 30 1
+0.700      move to 8 1
+0.700      move to 200 1
+0.700      move to 500 1
